desc: Dub Jeopardy Feedback Delay (mda DubDelay port) by chmaha
tags: delay echo dub feedback tape lfo
author: chmaha
version: 1.0
changelog:
  Initial release.
about:
  Dub-style feedback delay with up to several seconds of echo. Feedback runs from 0 to 110%: left of
  centre the feedback path saturates (soft clip), right of centre it is held back by a limiter, so you
  can push it past 100% and let the echoes build and smear without blowing up. Fb Tone tilts the
  feedback path: left darkens each repeat, right thins it out. The LFO wobbles the delay time for tape
  wow and pitch bends, and changing Delay while it plays gives the classic pitch-sliding dub throw.
  The echo path takes the left input only, as in the original; FX Mix keeps about -3 dB at 50%.
  Ported from mda DubDelay by Paul Kellett (Maxim Digital Audio), via mda-effects
  https://github.com/pluginguru/mda-effects (MIT or GPLv2+)
  JSFX version released under GPLv3+ license
  Claude generated some of this code
